  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "An analysis of satellite imagery from 1996 to 2023 alongside household surveys revealed that the built-up area of Robe town grew from 619.03 ha (6.55%) to 2089.27 ha (22.11%), while agricultural land contracted from 7959.06 ha (84.21%) to 6482.52 ha (68.59%). Land-change projections indicate that urban development will occupy 42.60% (4026.34 ha) of the study area by 2050, reducing farmland to 50.47% (4770.27 ha).",
      "why": "The study measures the precise trajectory of farmland loss in a rapidly growing Ethiopian secondary town, replacing general assumptions about peri-urban conversion with local spatial metrics."
